        {
          "id": "7c1579d1-6dfe-31ba-9c7e-a3f37b25bc5f",
          "content": {
            "id": "7c1579d1-6dfe-31ba-9c7e-a3f37b25bc5f",
            "contentType": "STORY",
            "title": "ReserveOne, backed by crypto heavyweights, set to raise over $1 billion in Nasdaq listing",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "(Reuters) -ReserveOne, a new crypto venture with ties to industry veterans and a former U.S. commerce secretary, will list on the Nasdaq through a merger with blank-check firm M3-Brigade Acquisition V Corp and is expected to raise more than $1 billion.  The company will manage a portfolio of cryptocurrencies including bitcoin, ethereum and Solana, while aligning its holdings with the U.S. strategic crypto reserve, it said on Tuesday.  The deal, expected to close in the October-December quarter, is the latest in a series of efforts to wrap crypto assets into equity and make them more appealing for traditional investors.",
